OL,3,AFirst human case of Shamonda virus
OL,4,Adetected in France, officials say
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe first known human case of the
OL,7,FShamonda virus (Shav) has been detected
OL,8,Fin a patient who died in early October,
OL,9,FFrench authorities have said.
OL,11,FHealth officials said it was an
OL,12,F"exceptional case in a severely
OL,13,Fimmunocompromised patient" and there
OL,14,Fwas currently no risk to the public.
OL,16,FShav is a disease that primarily
OL,17,Faffects cattle and can be spread by
OL,18,Finfected midges. Cases have also
OL,19,Foccurred in sheep, goats, alpacas and
OL,20,Fhorses, but infections in people were
OL,21,Fpreviously unheard of.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
